  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 145 PM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nThe active pattern will continue Tuesday night through Wednesday as \na secondary surface low that's progged to develop over southwestern \nKansas will sweep through the area late Tuesday, along with a \nsurface cold front. Accumulating rainfall appears to wane in the \nwake of the fropa, but we will remain under a cloudy and cool \npattern for the latter half of the week as a closed upper low is \nprogged to develop over the Midwest. Confidence in this occurring is \nquite high, given the general consensus among the LREF ensemble \ncluster analysis. So, we will be dealing with persistent cyclonic \nflow, some lingering spotty light rain showers and some breezy \nwinds, this time from the southwest. High temperatures on Thursday \nand Friday will cool down quite a bit compared to early this week \nbut will still remain above average for early November - in the \nupper 50s to lower 60s.\n\nFriday through the upcoming weekend: conditions look to become dry, \nalong with some peaks of sunshine here and there. This is thanks to \nan area of high pressure that is progged to build over the region \nbehind the departing cut-off low. High temperatures look to continue \nto warm into the upper 50s to near 60.",
